 an actor and that  you know uh dottie is just sarah it's a  problem i've seen a lot of shows  recently where i hope  show creators can understand that  audiences are  really really smart now and that's  because we watch so much damn tv  and we want more we want more for our  time and  there will be people that would defend  it and like whoa that's your fault and  like  you know it's it's silly the cool thing  twist is that there is no twist and that  you just over thought it  i'm not asking for a crazy reveal like  mephisto or magneto  flying down that would be awesome but no  i'm just asking for  you need to have things though that  shock people and throw people off that  make us feel like we're using our brain  a little more and i feel like that's  where the show kind of missed the mark  where in the beginning  you felt that it was setting up for  something that was making you use your  brain and try to figure everything out i  think that's why everyone got so excited  but when you don't pay it off that way  and it's just  more cut and dry brings it back down to  what most of these mcu projects are like  where it's just  solid but they didn't really go to where  the the ceiling was for this show that's  my biggest  disappointment of it all but having said  that  awesome acting all around the production  design is incredible the effort put into  every episode  with all the easter eggs really really  just amazing the music and in particular  catherine hahn was incredible as agatha  harkness and  elizabeth olsen just killed it  especially in this finale i thought in  particular  the scene where she's realizing what  she's done  to all these people and they all start  coming after her and then her snapping i  thought that was the best acting i've  actually ever seen elizabeth olsen do so  really props to her and like i said in  the beginning  we really need to consider emmys for  people even in superhero shows and that  starts here with elizabeth olsen  it's just inc